{"title":"Career Roadmap · Biostatistician","role":"Biostatistician","summary":"A Biostatistician applies statistical methods to biological, medical, pharmaceutical and public-health data. The role combines statistics, study design, data analysis and scientific interpretation to help answer questions such as whether a treatment works, how a disease is distributed, or whether an observed health effect is statistically meaningful.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc (Bachelor of Science – General / Honours)","Course":"Statistics"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Biostatistician applies statistical methods to biological, medical, pharmaceutical and public-health data. The role combines statistics, study design, data analysis and scientific interpretation to help answer questions such as whether a treatment works, how a disease is distributed, or whether an observed health effect is statistically meaningful."},{"type":"p","text":"Typical work includes:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Designing clinical studies and experiments"},{"text":"Determining appropriate sample sizes"},{"text":"Randomization and study design"},{"text":"Analyzing clinical and health datasets"},{"text":"Regression and survival analysis"},{"text":"Hypothesis testing"},{"text":"Confidence intervals and uncertainty analysis"},{"text":"Clinical-trial data analysis"},{"text":"Epidemiological analysis"},{"text":"Statistical programming"},{"text":"Preparing statistical reports"},{"text":"Communicating findings to medical/research teams"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For a B.Sc Statistics graduate, entry-level health-data, research-assistant or statistical-analyst roles are realistic. For a dedicated professional Biostatistician career, an M.Sc/M.Stat in Biostatistics, Statistics, or a closely related quantitative discipline is strongly recommended."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizon","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Career Development"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Statistics + probability + biology foundations"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Statistical inference + R/Python"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Biostatistics + epidemiology + research"}],[{"text":"0–2 years"},{"text":"Research Assistant / Statistical Analyst"}],[{"text":"2–5 years"},{"text":"Biostatistician / Junior Biostatistician"}],[{"text":"5–8 years"},{"text":"Senior Biostatistician"}],[{"text":"8+ years"},{"text":"Principal Biostatistician / Statistical Scientist"}]]},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc Statistics","Probability + Statistical Inference"]},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"flow","items":["Biology / Healthcare Fundamentals","R + Python + SQL","Biostatistics Projects","Research / Clinical Internship","M.Sc / M.Stat Biostatistics","Biostatistician","Senior Biostatistician","Principal / Lead Biostatistician"]}]},{"heading":"Year 1 — Statistical & Biological Foundations","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The first year should establish two foundations:"},{"type":"h","text":"Statistics + Life Sciences"},{"type":"h","text":"Statistics"},{"type":"p","text":"Build strong understanding of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Descriptive statistics"},{"text":"Probability"},{"text":"Random variables"},{"text":"Probability distributions"},{"text":"Expectation"},{"text":"Variance"},{"text":"Covariance"},{"text":"Sampling"},{"text":"Correlation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Important distributions:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Bernoulli"},{"text":"Binomial"},{"text":"Poisson"},{"text":"Normal"},{"text":"Exponential"},{"text":"t-distribution"},{"text":"Chi-square"},{"text":"F-distribution"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Mathematics"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Calculus"},{"text":"Linear algebra"},{"text":"Mathematical reasoning"},{"text":"Basic differential equations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Biology foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"A statistics student entering biostatistics should understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cell biology"},{"text":"Genetics"},{"text":"Human anatomy basics"},{"text":"Physiology"},{"text":"Microbiology fundamentals"},{"text":"Disease concepts"},{"text":"Basic molecular biology"},{"text":"The objective is not to become a medical professional, but to understand the scientific context behind healthcare data."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Statistical Inference & Programming"},{"type":"p","text":"This is where the student starts becoming capable of real statistical analysis."},{"type":"h","text":"Statistical inference"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Point estimation"},{"text":"Interval estimation"},{"text":"Confidence intervals"},{"text":"Hypothesis testing"},{"text":"p-values"},{"text":"Statistical power"},{"text":"Effect size"},{"text":"Type I and Type II errors"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Statistical tests"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand when and why to use:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"t-test"},{"text":"Chi-square test"},{"text":"ANOVA"},{"text":"Non-parametric tests"},{"text":"Correlation tests"},{"text":"Regression"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Do not memorize tests as isolated formulas. Learn:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Research Question","Data Type","Study Design","Statistical Assumptions","Appropriate Test / Model","Result","Interpretation"]}]},{"heading":"Statistical Programming","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"R — Primary Skill"},{"type":"p","text":"R is particularly important for biostatistics."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"R fundamentals"},{"text":"Data frames"},{"text":"Data manipulation"},{"text":"ggplot2"},{"text":"dplyr"},{"text":"tidyr"},{"text":"Statistical modelling"},{"text":"Reproducible reports"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Useful packages include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"tidyverse"},{"text":"survival"},{"text":"lme4"},{"text":"broom"},{"text":"ggplot2"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Python"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Python fundamentals"},{"text":"NumPy"},{"text":"pandas"},{"text":"SciPy"},{"text":"statsmodels"},{"text":"matplotlib"}]},{"type":"h","text":"SQL"},{"type":"p","text":"Useful for healthcare databases and large datasets:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"SELECT"},{"text":"JOIN"},{"text":"GROUP BY"},{"text":"CTEs"},{"text":"Window functions"},{"text":"Aggregation"}]}]},{"heading":"Year 3 — Core Biostatistics","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The third year should become strongly specialized toward healthcare research."},{"type":"h","text":"Regression"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Linear regression"},{"text":"Multiple regression"},{"text":"Logistic regression"},{"text":"Poisson regression"},{"text":"Generalized linear models"},{"text":"Model diagnostics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Survival analysis"},{"type":"p","text":"Very important for medical research."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Survival function"},{"text":"Hazard function"},{"text":"Censoring"},{"text":"Kaplan-Meier curves"},{"text":"Log-rank test"},{"text":"Cox proportional hazards model"}]},{"type":"flow","items":["Patient Data","Follow-up Period","Event / Censoring","Survival Analysis","Kaplan-Meier / Cox Model","Hazard / Survival Estimates"]},{"type":"h","text":"Longitudinal data"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Repeated measurements"},{"text":"Mixed-effects models"},{"text":"Correlated observations"},{"text":"Longitudinal study design"}]}]},{"heading":"Clinical Trial Fundamentals","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A biostatistician should understand the structure of clinical research."},{"type":"flow","items":["Research Question","Study Protocol","Eligibility Criteria","Sample Size","Randomization","Treatment / Control","Data Collection","Statistical Analysis","Safety + Efficacy","Final Report"]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Clinical trial phases"},{"text":"Randomized controlled trials"},{"text":"Control groups"},{"text":"Blinding"},{"text":"Randomization"},{"text":"Endpoints"},{"text":"Inclusion/exclusion criteria"},{"text":"Treatment effects"},{"text":"Adverse events"},{"text":"Missing data"},{"text":"Protocol deviations"}]}]},{"heading":"Core Biostatistical Concepts","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Concept","Importance"],"rows":[[{"text":"Probability"},{"text":"Very High"}],[{"text":"Statistical Inference"},{"text":"Very High"}],[{"text":"Regression"},{"text":"Very High"}],[{"text":"Experimental Design"},{"text":"Very High"}],[{"text":"Clinical Trial Design"},{"text":"Very High"}],[{"text":"Survival Analysis"},{"text":"Very High"}],[{"text":"Epidemiology"},{"text":"High"}],[{"text":"Sampling"},{"text":"High"}],[{"text":"Longitudinal Analysis"},{"text":"High"}],[{"text":"Missing Data"},{"text":"High"}],[{"text":"Causal Inference"},{"text":"High"}],[{"text":"Statistical Programming"},{"text":"Very High"}],[{"text":"Scientific Communication"},{"text":"Very High"}]]}]},{"heading":"Study Design Knowledge","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Biostatistics is not just about analyzing datasets after someone else collects them."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn the difference between:"},{"type":"h","text":"Observational studies"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cross-sectional studies"},{"text":"Case-control studies"},{"text":"Cohort studies"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Experimental studies"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Randomized controlled trials"},{"text":"Factorial designs"},{"text":"Crossover studies"},{"text":"Cluster randomized trials"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Epidemiological workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["Population","Study Design","Sample Selection","Exposure / Intervention","Outcome Measurement","Statistical Analysis","Association / Effect","Scientific Interpretation"]}]},{"heading":"Major Projects","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — Clinical Trial Analysis"},{"type":"p","text":"Use a public or simulated clinical dataset."},{"type":"p","text":"Analyze:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Treatment groups"},{"text":"Baseline characteristics"},{"text":"Primary endpoint"},{"text":"Secondary endpoints"},{"text":"Confidence intervals"},{"text":"Effect size"},{"text":"Statistical significance"},{"text":"Produce a mock statistical report."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — Survival Analysis"},{"type":"p","text":"Analyze patient survival data."},{"type":"p","text":"Implement:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Kaplan-Meier curves"},{"text":"Survival probabilities"},{"text":"Log-rank test"},{"text":"Cox proportional hazards model"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Example:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Patient Dataset","Time-to-Event Variable","Censoring Identification","Kaplan-Meier","Cox Regression","Hazard Ratio","Interpretation"]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3 — Disease Risk Model"},{"type":"p","text":"Build a logistic regression model to estimate disease risk."},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Odds ratios"},{"text":"Confidence intervals"},{"text":"Predictors"},{"text":"Model fit"},{"text":"Classification performance"},{"text":"Avoid claiming that a statistical association proves causation."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 4 — Epidemiological Study"},{"type":"p","text":"Analyze a public health dataset involving:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Disease prevalence"},{"text":"Risk factors"},{"text":"Demographic variables"},{"text":"Geographic variables"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Calculate:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Prevalence"},{"text":"Relative risk"},{"text":"Odds ratio"},{"text":"Confidence intervals"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 5 — Longitudinal Patient Data"},{"type":"p","text":"Analyze repeated measurements such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Blood pressure"},{"text":"Glucose"},{"text":"Weight"},{"text":"Biomarkers"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Patient","Visit 1","Visit 2","Visit 3","Visit 4","Repeated Measures","Mixed-Effects Model"]}]},{"heading":"Internship Roadmap","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"After Year 1"},{"type":"p","text":"Look for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"University research projects"},{"text":"Public-health projects"},{"text":"Biology/statistics research groups"},{"text":"Data-analysis internships"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Statistics","R","basic biology"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"After Year 2"},{"type":"p","text":"Target:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Hospitals with research units"},{"text":"Public-health organizations"},{"text":"Pharmaceutical companies"},{"text":"CROs"},{"text":"Academic medical research groups"},{"text":"Epidemiology research teams"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Possible roles:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research Intern"},{"text":"Biostatistics Intern"},{"text":"Statistical Intern"},{"text":"Health Data Analyst Intern"},{"text":"Clinical Research Intern"}]},{"type":"h","text":"After Year 3"},{"type":"p","text":"Prioritize internships involving:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Clinical trials"},{"text":"Survival analysis"},{"text":"Epidemiological studies"},{"text":"Statistical programming"},{"text":"Healthcare datasets"},{"text":"Research methodology"},{"text":"A good internship should expose the student to real study design and statistical reasoning, not merely Excel data entry."}]}]},{"heading":"Entry-Level Career Options","kind":"careers","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"After the appropriate qualification, possible roles include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Junior Biostatistician"},{"text":"Biostatistician"},{"text":"Statistical Analyst"},{"text":"Biostatistics Analyst"},{"text":"Clinical Data Analyst"},{"text":"Statistical Programmer"},{"text":"Research Analyst"},{"text":"Clinical Research Analyst"},{"text":"Research Assistant"},{"text":"Epidemiology Data Analyst"},{"text":"Public Health Data Analyst"},{"text":"Healthcare Data Analyst"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For advanced roles such as Senior Biostatistician, Statistical Scientist or Lead Biostatistician, postgraduate qualifications and relevant experience are generally expected."}]},{"heading":"Employer / Industry Skill Matrix","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Industry","Important Skills"],"rows":[[{"text":"Pharmaceutical"},{"text":"Clinical trials, R, SAS familiarity"}],[{"text":"CRO"},{"text":"Statistical programming, clinical studies"}],[{"text":"Hospitals"},{"text":"Clinical research, epidemiology"}],[{"text":"Public Health"},{"text":"Epidemiology, survey statistics"}],[{"text":"Biotechnology"},{"text":"Experimental statistics"}],[{"text":"Medical Research"},{"text":"Survival analysis, regression"}],[{"text":"Academic Research"},{"text":"Statistical inference + research"}],[{"text":"Health Technology"},{"text":"Statistics + healthcare data"}],[{"text":"Government"},{"text":"Survey and population statistics"}],[{"text":"Epidemiology"},{"text":"Study design + causal reasoning"}]]}]},{"heading":"SAS & Statistical Software","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"R"},{"type":"p","text":"Should be a major priority."},{"type":"h","text":"SAS"},{"type":"p","text":"SAS remains relevant in many pharmaceutical and clinical-research environments."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"SAS programming fundamentals"},{"text":"DATA steps"},{"text":"PROC procedures"},{"text":"Dataset manipulation"},{"text":"Statistical procedures"},{"text":"Reporting"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Python"},{"type":"p","text":"Useful for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Data processing"},{"text":"Automation"},{"text":"Machine learning"},{"text":"Statistical analysis"},{"text":"Visualization"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Specialized tools"},{"type":"p","text":"Become familiar with the purpose of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"REDCap-type research data systems"},{"text":"Electronic data capture"},{"text":"Clinical trial databases"},{"text":"LIMS"},{"text":"Statistical reporting workflows"}]}]},{"heading":"Data Quality & Missing Data","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Healthcare data is rarely perfect."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to handle:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Missing observations"},{"text":"Outliers"},{"text":"Measurement errors"},{"text":"Duplicate records"},{"text":"Inconsistent coding"},{"text":"Censored observations"},{"text":"Loss to follow-up"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand concepts such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MCAR"},{"text":"MAR"},{"text":"MNAR"},{"text":"Multiple imputation"},{"text":"Sensitivity analysis"},{"text":"A good biostatistician should never silently remove inconvenient observations just to improve the model."}]}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Training","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Useful training areas include:"},{"type":"h","text":"Statistics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Biostatistics"},{"text":"Regression"},{"text":"Survival analysis"},{"text":"Experimental design"},{"text":"Bayesian statistics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical research"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Clinical trial methodology"},{"text":"Good Clinical Practice (GCP) awareness"},{"text":"Clinical research methodology"},{"text":"Research ethics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Programming"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"R"},{"text":"SAS"},{"text":"Python"},{"text":"SQL"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Epidemiology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Epidemiological methods"},{"text":"Public health statistics"},{"text":"Study design"},{"text":"Certificates should support actual skills and project experience rather than substitute for them."}]}]},{"heading":"Higher Education Path","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"M.Sc / M.Stat in Biostatistics"},{"type":"p","text":"Strongly recommended for a dedicated Biostatistician career."},{"type":"p","text":"Possible postgraduate areas:"},{"type":"table","header":["PG Specialization","Career Direction"],"rows":[[{"text":"Biostatistics"},{"text":"Clinical / Medical Research"}],[{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Broad statistical careers"}],[{"text":"Medical Statistics"},{"text":"Healthcare"}],[{"text":"Epidemiology"},{"text":"Public Health"}],[{"text":"Bioinformatics"},{"text":"Computational Biology"}],[{"text":"Data Science"},{"text":"Health Data / AI"}],[{"text":"Public Health"},{"text":"Population-level research"}]]}]},{"heading":"Advanced Research Path","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc Statistics","M.Sc / M.Stat Biostatistics","Research / Clinical Internship","Biostatistician","Advanced Statistical Research","PhD","Statistical Scientist / Researcher"]},{"type":"p","text":"A PhD becomes particularly valuable for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Academic research"},{"text":"Advanced methodology"},{"text":"Statistical genetics"},{"text":"Clinical-trial methodology"},{"text":"Causal inference research"},{"text":"Independent research leadership"}]}]},{"heading":"Specialization Paths","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Path 1 — Clinical Trials"},{"type":"flow","items":["Statistics","Biostatistics","Clinical Trial Design","Statistical Programming","Biostatistician","Senior / Lead Biostatistician"]},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"R/SAS"},{"text":"Clinical trial design"},{"text":"Survival analysis"},{"text":"Regulatory statistical reporting"},{"text":"Missing data"},{"text":"Repeated measures"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Path 2 — Epidemiology & Public Health"},{"type":"flow","items":["Statistics","Biostatistics"]},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"flow","items":["Epidemiology","Population Data","Public Health Analyst","Epidemiological Statistician"]},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cohort studies"},{"text":"Case-control studies"},{"text":"Survey design"},{"text":"Disease surveillance"},{"text":"Risk estimation"},{"text":"Causal inference"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Path 3 — Pharmaceutical R&D"},{"type":"flow","items":["Statistics","Biostatistics","Pharmaceutical Research","Clinical Development","Biostatistician","Statistical Scientist"]},{"type":"p","text":"Add:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Clinical trial methodology"},{"text":"GCP awareness"},{"text":"SAS"},{"text":"R"},{"text":"Regulatory documentation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Path 4 — Bioinformatics & Computational Biology"},{"type":"flow","items":["Statistics","Biostatistics","Python + R","Genomics / Bioinformatics","Computational Biologist","Quantitative Biology"]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Genomics"},{"text":"Transcriptomics"},{"text":"High-dimensional data"},{"text":"Machine learning"},{"text":"Statistical genetics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Path 5 — Statistical Research"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc Statistics","M.Sc / M.Stat","Research","PhD","Statistical Scientist","Research Lead"]},{"type":"p","text":"Potential research areas:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Causal inference"},{"text":"Bayesian biostatistics"},{"text":"Survival analysis"},{"text":"Longitudinal modelling"},{"text":"Statistical genetics"},{"text":"Clinical trial methodology"}]}]},{"heading":"Emerging Technologies","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"AI + Biostatistics"},{"type":"p","text":"AI can assist with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Patient risk modelling"},{"text":"Clinical data analysis"},{"text":"Trial optimization"},{"text":"Biomarker discovery"},{"text":"Medical prediction"},{"text":"Automated statistical workflows"},{"text":"However, statistical validation remains essential."}]},{"type":"flow","items":["Healthcare Data","Statistical Analysis","Machine Learning","Model Validation","Uncertainty / Bias Analysis","Clinical Interpretation"]},{"type":"h","text":"Emerging areas"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Causal AI"},{"text":"Federated learning"},{"text":"Synthetic clinical data"},{"text":"Real-world evidence"},{"text":"Digital health analytics"},{"text":"Statistical genetics"},{"text":"Multi-omics analysis"},{"text":"AI-assisted clinical trials"},{"text":"Bayesian adaptive trials"}]}]},{"heading":"Recommended Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Minimum employability stack"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"B.Sc Statistics"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Probability"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Statistical Inference"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Regression"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Biostatistics Fundamentals"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"R"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Python"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"SQL"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Healthcare Data"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Strong Biostatistician profile"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Biostatistics"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Clinical Trial Design"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Regression"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Survival Analysis"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"R + SAS"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Python + SQL"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Research Experience"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced 2026+ profile"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Biostatistics"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Causal Inference"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Bayesian Methods"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Survival Analysis"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Clinical Trials"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"R / SAS / Python"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Real-World Evidence"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Machine Learning"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"AI Model Evaluation"}]}]},{"heading":"Target Profile by Graduation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"By the end of B.Sc, a strong candidate should be able to:"},{"type":"h","text":"Statistical"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Perform descriptive analysis"},{"text":"Conduct hypothesis tests"},{"text":"Build regression models"},{"text":"Interpret confidence intervals"},{"text":"Understand statistical power"},{"text":"Understand study design"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Biostatistical"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Explain clinical trial structure"},{"text":"Understand epidemiological study types"},{"text":"Perform basic survival analysis"},{"text":"Understand risk ratios and odds ratios"},{"text":"Handle healthcare datasets"},{"text":"Recognize confounding and bias"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Programming"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"R"},{"text":"Python"},{"text":"SQL"},{"text":"pandas"},{"text":"SciPy"},{"text":"statsmodels"},{"text":"R statistical packages"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Read scientific papers"},{"text":"Formulate statistical questions"},{"text":"Select appropriate methods"},{"text":"Document analytical decisions"},{"text":"Produce reproducible reports"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Portfolio"},{"type":"p","text":"Build at least 4–6 projects, including:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Clinical trial analysis"},{"text":"Survival analysis"},{"text":"Logistic regression/disease-risk study"},{"text":"Epidemiological analysis"},{"text":"Longitudinal data analysis"},{"text":"Healthcare data visualization/reporting"}]}]},{"heading":"Best Overall Positioning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The strongest profile is not simply:"},{"type":"h","text":"B.Sc Statistics → Biostatistician"},{"type":"p","text":"Instead:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Statistics","Biostatistics","Clinical Research","Statistical Programming"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"The recommended progression is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc Statistics","Probability + Statistical Inference","Biostatistics + Epidemiology","R + SAS + Python + SQL","Clinical / Healthcare Projects","Research Internship","M.Sc / M.Stat Biostatistics","Biostatistician","Senior Biostatistician","Lead / Principal Biostatistician"]},{"type":"note","label":"Core positioning","text":"Biostatistician with strong statistical foundations, clinical-study knowledge, R/SAS programming, survival analysis and healthcare-domain expertise."},{"type":"p","text":"For a student specifically targeting professional biostatistics rather than generic data analytics, postgraduate specialization in Biostatistics/Statistics is one of the most valuable steps after B.Sc Statistics."}]}]}